From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 20:00:00 -0700
Subject: cam: isp: raise CAM_ISP_CTX_REQ_MAX to 20 for camerad's queue depth

camerad keeps VIPC_BUFFER_COUNT (18) requests in flight per camera;
camera_kt's per-context ISP request pool is only 8, so the startup
requeue exhausts it ("No more request obj free", CONFIG_DEV -> ENOMEM)
before the first frame can complete. The generic cam_context pool
(CAM_CTX_REQ_MAX) is already 20 and the legacy 4.9 kernel this
userspace was built against accepted the full depth. Match it.
---

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h
index f885920..dc97523 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 #define CAM_ISP_CTX_RES_MAX                     24
 
 /* max requests per ctx for isp */
-#define CAM_ISP_CTX_REQ_MAX                     8
+#define CAM_ISP_CTX_REQ_MAX                     20
 
 /*
  * Maximum entries in state monitoring array for error logging
